<title>USA: Target gets okay to sell device in Japan.</title>
<headline>Target gets okay to sell device in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Target Therapeutics Inc said Friday it had won approval to market in Japan its first-generation Guglielmi Detachable Coli device.</p>
<p>The device is designed for minimally invasive treatment of intracranial aneurysms and neurovascular lesions that are either inoperable or require high-risk surgery. Its use has significantly reduced mortality and recurrence in stroke victims since its international launch in fiscal 1995, Target said.</p>
<p>The device was launched in the U.S. a year ago.</p>
<p>Target stock was up 1-9/16 at 39-3/8 in early trading.</p>
</text>
